# Cursor Rules — streamlit-trading-dashboard

## Project
Streamlit dashboard + SQL view creator + daily signal tracking/AI predictions for stock trading platform.

## Stack
- Python 3.11+, Streamlit, pandas, plotly, pyodbc, scikit-learn
- SQL Server (localhost\MSSQLSERVER01, stockdata_db)

## Architecture
- app.py — 11,658-line monolithic Streamlit app (15 pages)
- create_views.py — Creates 40+ SQL views for ecosystem
- daily_prediction_job.py — Daily per market: 7-day UP/FLAT/DOWN direction classifier
  (LightGBM + LogisticRegression, retrained from scratch every run; no pickled artifact).
  predicted_price is a volatility proxy, NOT a forecast — do not report MAE/RMSE as model error.
- signal_tracker.py — Daily 7 PM: Signal outcome tracking

## Critical Views Created
- vw_PowerBI_AI_Technical_Combos (TIER 1/2 signals — used by agentic AI)
- vw_strategy2_trade_opportunities (Trade grades A-D — used by agentic AI)
- Per-market indicator views (RSI, MACD, BB, ATR, Stochastic, Fibonacci, S/R, Patterns)
- Per-market signal views + crossover aggregates
- Fundamental screening views

## Tables Written
- ai_prediction_history, signal_tracking_history, daily_signals_history

## Schedule
- 6:00 PM daily AI predictions
- 7:00 PM daily signal tracking

## Known Issues
- app.py is monolithic (11,658 lines) — decompose into pages/
- SQL credentials hardcoded — move to .env
- No automated tests

## Ecosystem
Views from this repo are consumed by stockdata_agenticai agents, ML pipelines, and sqlserver_mcp.
- sqlserver_mcp — .NET 8 MCP Server (Microsoft MssqlMcp): 7 tools (ListTables, DescribeTable, ReadData, CreateTable, DropTable, InsertData, UpdateData) via stdio. Use to explore DB schemas/data during development.

